    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345-a3">

                <pb facs="0510" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg414"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 3—Translation<anchor n="26"
                            xml:id="d345-f1"/>]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Secretary of Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Pani</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9,
                        1921</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Summerlin</hi>: I have the pleasure to
                    refer to your letter of the 7th instant, with which I received the summary of
                    one of the telegrams sent by you to the Department of State in Washington, in
                    connection with the conversation which we held on Saturday last in regard to
                    memorandum no. 2.</p>
                <p>With this letter I transmit the summary referred to, after having made some small
                    indispensable modifications to make it agree exactly with my statements.</p>
                <p>I remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. Pani</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
